WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations
on your Emmy nomination.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very exciting.
-It is exciting.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:05.505
-So, this show was inspired
by a book you wrote in 2015,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Troublemaker," that sort of
detailed your experience

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.709 line:92%
with the Church of Scientology.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sorry. I'm futzing
because I just ripped my dress

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the dressing room.
-Oh, really?

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:17.083
-Do you think -- Do you think --
Did the Scientologists do it?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.688 line:92%
Yeah, it's a plot, it's a plot.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so,
it was actually inspired

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
from other people
telling their stories.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.060 line:92%
-Because once you wrote --

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.763
Is it fair to say, safe to say,
that once you wrote your book

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
about your experience,
you were approached

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
by a lot of other people
that had a similar experience?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.668 line:92%
-Well, yes, but also, you know,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's one thing
to leave Scientology.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's another thing
to speak out publicly,

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I knew
that I had to do that,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.110
because Scientology
has a policy that if you leave,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can leave, but you just
have to leave quietly.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:50.784
If you publicly speak out,
then they label you an enemy,

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.485 line:92%
and then they start to attack.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I knew
that I had to do something

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
to let people know on the
outside that I was with them.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And one of the things
you talk about

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
that came up a lot
in the first season

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.729 line:92%
is this idea of disconnecting.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.632
Can you explain what that is
and how Scientology uses that?

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.134
-Yes. Like I said,
if you leave and speak publicly,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
then anybody in your family,
all your friends,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
would have
to disconnect from you.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.007 line:92%
They shun you, basically.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's
what disconnection is.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.310 size:78% position:39%
And I was seeing that
over and over again.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, I knew the policies
of Scientology when I --

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.481 line:92%
'Cause I was raised in it.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I actually
never saw it happen.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.387 size:84% position:42%
You know, you grow up
in Scientology thinking

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's us against them"
mentality.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:33.626
And it's a slow indoctrination
into this brainwashing cult.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:39.566
But I should probably be kinder
so early on in the show, but --

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you do --
Now, you have --

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.703
You know, it seems like there is
more and more information

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what Scientology is
and I think maybe

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.209 line:92%
a little bit warning about it

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.177 size:75% position:38%
more than there were
in previous years.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yet it seems to be,
according to you,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.415 line:92%
that people within Scientology

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
are not exposed
to that information.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does Scientology
sort of control

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
what people within it
are exposed to

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.790 line:92%
and what they're reading?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good question. Uh...
Yeah.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sit on that for a second.
Yeah.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.029 line:92%
How -- How does it happen?

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
It happens by, very early on
in your indoctrination,

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
this mentality that
"It's us against them."

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't read the newspapers.
Don't watch television.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't listen
to critics of Scientology."

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.343
And they have all this
information on people who leave.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.845
They were
doing weird things with animals.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.913 line:92%
They have packets on them.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "Wha?
Joe was doing that?"

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.216 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And so they're, like,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
"yeah, you can't call him,
though, to verify it,

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
because if you call Joe
and ask him..."

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
We've one of those guys here.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you do?
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
His name Joe?
-I shouldn't say, but...

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.062 line:92%
So, you know, you're not allowed

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
to speak to people
once they leave,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
so there's no verifying
that information.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.600 size:75% position:38% line:92%
If you do call them,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
then you're interrogated
at your expense,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're put
on a lie detector.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there's
a lot of repercussions

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
to looking outside of the
organization for information.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you're just
not allowed to do that.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that answer the question,
or are you still like,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, but why didn't
you still look?"

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
And I understand.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
Certainly, also, it seems,
what you're stressing,

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.522
which makes a lot of sense,
is this all happens slowly.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you, I think,
were raised into it,

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
but people get into it
even later in life.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It must seem like
a very nice, helpful thing.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.597
I can't imagine your early time
in Scientology is negative.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, of course.
In the beginning, it's like

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.201 line:92%
you learn how to talk to people.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at them in the eye
when you're talking to them.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do little courses
on finances

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.807 line:92%
and how to achieve your goals.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.276 line:92%
You know, $35, $45 courses.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.811 line:92%
And as you go on, you know,

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you go proposition --
right? --

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:37.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're in at $250,000
by the time you're done,

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.086 line:92%
and I'm being, again, very kind.

